WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.935
-Our next guest is a very
talented actress you know

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.805
from shows like "Parks and
Recreation" and "Good Girls."

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.475
She hosts
"Ugliest House in America,"

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.178
which airs Sunday nights on HGTV
and streams on Discovery Plus.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.580
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.114
-There are some bugs
in there and --

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.349
-A lot.
-A lot.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.251
There was spiders,
all kinds of stuff.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:20.787
-Yep.
-Lizards.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.987 line:0%
-Lizards?!
-Lizards.

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:24.758 line:0%
-In the house?!
-In the walls.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.559 line:0%
-So this is why
you ripped up this room?

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.394 line:0%
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.931
-Oh, if it was my house,
I'd kill it with fire.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.200
[Hushed]
Burn it to the ground!

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.635
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.603
our friend Retta, everybody!

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.672
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:48.047 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:56.455 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:58.490
Welcome back, Retta!

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.027
You are -- You're one
of our favorite guests,

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:03.462
and the last couple of times
we've been talking virtually.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.564
So it's so lovely to have you
back here in studio.

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:06.866
-It's nice to be back.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.036
-This is such a fun idea
for a show.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.138
This is -- A third season's
just been announced.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.906
-Yes.
-When they first reached out

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.409
and asked you to host this show,
were you excited about the idea

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.643
of being a host?
-No.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.912
-Okay.
-No. I don't --

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.348
I have anxiety about hosting.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.450
I'm like -- I don't know
if I'm giving it my all.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.953
And then HGTV is like
a different beast, you know.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.888
I used to hate
hosting comedy shows.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.256
-Yep.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.558
-I was like -- it's hard to be
a cheerleader all night.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:34.460
[ Laughter ]
So when they asked me

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.563
to do this,
I was a little bit nervous.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.798
And then it's like, "You're
making fun of people's homes."

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.766
And they were like, "Relax.
They submitted their homes."

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:41.868
-Yeah.
-So...

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.370
-I guess you don't
have to be a cheerleader

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.640
when people literally think they
have one of the ugliest homes.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.642
-You're like, "Yeah.
You're right. This is trash."

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.611
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:55.247
-Now, in the clip,
they were talking about having

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:58.017
a lizard problem
in their home, a insect problem.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.552
Is this a recurring theme
in the homes you see?

00:02:00.552 --> 00:02:03.623
Animals? Animal life?

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.491
-Yes.
-[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:10.830
So, first season, this one
family is telling me how --

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.832
They're like, "Yeah, we were
just sitting down watching TV

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.067
and a snake
fell out of the ceiling."

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.569
And I was like, "What?!"

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.936
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.936 --> 00:02:20.473
And then we go
to the living room, we start --

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.174
And something falls
from the ceiling.

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:23.843
And I [bleep] myself.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.778
[ Laughter ]
I nearly passed out.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.279
And I was like, "What?!"

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:30.249
And it was just a piece
of the ceiling.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:33.018
We started season 3
a little while ago.

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:38.157
Two days ago, I'm in a house,
and this family tells me

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.227
that the daughter and father
were bonding

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.230
on the fact
that the daughter likes snakes.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.798
-Okay.
-And I was like,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.666
"Wow. Is that right?"

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:51.104
So then they were like, "Yeah,"
and they kind of got into it.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.305
And it was one snake,
and then it was two.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:56.075
And then my producer was like,
"Ask how many snakes."

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.411
And I was like --
Which made me panic.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.613
I was like, "Ask how many?!

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.947
He said two. There's more?

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.583
I feel like I already
got the answer."

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.217
I was like,
"How many snakes do you have?"

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:06.352
They were like, "26."

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.620
I was like, "What?!"

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.588
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.557
And then he was like,
"You want to see?"

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.561
And I was like, "Homey, no.
I don't want to see."

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.295
And all through the tour
he kept asking.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.431
I was like, "sir! No!"

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.733
-At least --
I feel like at least his snakes

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.735
were probably
in some sort of case

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.336
as opposed to a ceiling snake.

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:26.105
-That is true.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.809
But there's nothing but stories
of -- about snakes escaping.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.177
-Yeah, that's true.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.511
-And that's what
I wanted no part of.

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.846
-Yeah, when they were like,
"Here's all twenty si--

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.547
There's only 25 here."

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:38.484
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.852
-"Oh, yeah.
The big one's missing.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.554
The big one's
definitely not here."

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.590
-You're always short on snakes.
-You drive house to house.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.360
Has it been fun to be
on a road trip for this show?

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.030
-Again, no.
-Okay. Your honesty.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.700
-Because we basically
check into a hotel at night.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:59.539
We wake up, check out,
go to work, shoot all day,

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:03.409
drive two to four hours,
check in, go to sleep,

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.677
wake up, check out -- it's that.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:08.147
And I guess part of the drive
is you can't be like,

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:12.651
"Don't worry. We're on our way
to see a super-ugly house!"

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.720
What's the ugliest non-animal,

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.956
non-snake-themed thing
you've seen?

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:20.360
-Well, one of the things
that makes me crazy

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.329
is I can't get over the fact

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:27.066
how popular carpeting
in bathrooms was.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.368
-Yeah.
-Carpeting.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:32.171
-Mm-hmm.
-Not rugs.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.740
Carpeting.
-Yeah.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.909
Like, it seems like carpeting --
it takes so much longer

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.045
to put down that it's crazy
that while they were, like,

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:41.247
cutting it out around the toilet
someone wasn't like,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.548
"Oh, this is a terrible idea.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.517
I feel like
we should stop right now

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.452
while I have this
X-ACTO knife out."

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:50.189
-And not every bathroom
has a fan.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.859
So I get in there and I'm like,
"Have you checked for mold?"

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:55.461
And they're like, "No, we..."

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.129
I was like,
"You never checked for mold?"

00:04:57.129 --> 00:05:00.066
And I was like,
"We gotta wrap it up!"

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.870
But there was one house --
it was on Sunday's episode --

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:08.974
where they built the house
around a red rock.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:12.411
So for three stories up
there's just a giant rock.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.846
And they didn't seal it well.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.014
-Oh, wow.

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:18.818
So there's, like, some
breezy feelings off the rock?

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.452
-And critters.
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:22.021
-Yeah.
-Critters love a rock.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.756
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.726
Do you at least stay
at nice hotels over this tour?

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.729
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:32.331
I feel like this
is the longest streak of no's

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.633
I've ever had with a guest.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:37.135
-No.
No, because sometimes --

00:05:37.135 --> 00:05:40.506
A lot of these places are
just way out in no-man's land.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.041
-Yeah, sometimes
super-ugly houses

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.509
aren't right next
to the Four Seasons.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.644
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.246
So we're looking on Yelp.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:50.716
We're like, "Two stars!
Hallelujah!" You know?

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:53.052
-What's the second star for?

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.354
They're like,
"They felt bad for us."

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:56.955
-Exactly.
-"Yeah, the first star

00:05:56.955 --> 00:05:58.357
was because we had a door,

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.860
and the second star was
because they felt bad for us."

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.263
-"The first star is that
we had running water."

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:08.801
[ Sighs ] God. It's --
It is a true challenge.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.270
But I feel like
I shall persevere.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.939
-What about -- Have you lived
in ugly houses yourself,

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:16.075
like, independent of the show?

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.378
-Well, I mean, so,
my parents' current house,

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.214
when they bought it --
It was my parents' first house.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:25.017
-Yeah.
-You know, they were immigrants.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.619
They did not have
a lot of money.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.221
So they bought
their first house.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.255
They were so happy and so proud.

00:06:30.255 --> 00:06:33.025
And we were like,
"We're moving to a house!"

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:36.162
And then my parents took us
to see the house,

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:39.264
and I walked in.

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:41.333
The funk from
when they opened the door.

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:43.002
And I was like, "What is this?"

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:46.105
And my mother was like,
"Well, they had six dogs

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:48.240
that never left the house."

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.510
Never left the house.
-Never left the house.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.245
-No. So they did everything --
-Some lazy dogs.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.647
-And carpeting.

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:57.083
-Carpeting. Oh, no.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.318
-That was about
as thin as this now.

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.921
Because it had been shag,
and then it made its way --

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.457
[ Laughter ]
And it was really crazy.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:06.258
So, I remember
my parents were so proud.

00:07:06.258 --> 00:07:07.860
I just remember, like,
crying on the ride

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.328
back to our apartment, like,

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.964
"Oh, my God. I can't believe..."

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:15.000
I mean, they did, you know,
work before we moved in.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.502
And I'm allergic to dogs.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:19.304
So I was like, "I'm going to
choke to death in this house."

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:20.872
But they cleaned it up.
-Alright. That's nice.

00:07:20.872 --> 00:07:22.274
-I made it to "Seth."

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:24.877
-I found out --
When I was young, I found out

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:29.282
I was allergic to dogs,
and we had a dog.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:30.883
And my dad was like, "Yeah.

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:34.186
We're just going to
get you an inhaler."

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:36.121
He was like,
"I'm not getting rid of the dog,

00:07:36.121 --> 00:07:37.890
but I can get you an inhaler.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.459
You want an inhaler?

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:41.427
You want to be a cool kid
with an inhaler?"

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:43.195
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:45.831
-Did you get multiple dogs?
-Not only did we get

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:48.601
multiple dogs, but
I'm on my like 100th inhaler.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.536
[ Laughter ]
Now, I've seen --

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:53.905
Your current home on Zoom
looks very lovely.

00:07:53.905 --> 00:07:56.509
And you've sort of leaned
into sort of smart technology.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.810
Is that --
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.679
-I can't do it.
Do you like it?

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:02.148
-Yes. "Yes"!

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:03.282
-You do? Oh, we did it.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.084
[ Applause ]

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.686
We did it. Home stretch.

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:08.087
[ Applause ]

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:11.857
-Yes. I kind of
can't live without it.

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:14.527
It's like, you know, the first
time you fly first class

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:16.095
and then you have to
fly coach again.

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:18.396
You're like --
[ Breathes deeply, sobs ]

00:08:18.396 --> 00:08:20.733
"No more elbow room?"

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:23.836
Well, I literally get in bed --
I mean, at this point

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:27.806
I did disconnect
the alarm system from it

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:29.407
because I was like,

00:08:29.407 --> 00:08:32.177
"That's real risky to be like,
"Turn off the alarm!"

00:08:32.177 --> 00:08:35.013
When somebody comes in,
it's like, "Turn off the alarm!"

00:08:35.013 --> 00:08:36.882
-Yeah.
-And then they got me.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:38.584
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:43.222
But I do -- Every --
I talk to Google and Alexa.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:45.891
-You have two.
-In each room.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:48.494
In case one's being a little,
you know, problematic.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:49.862
-Withholding.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.631
-I'll be like,
"Oh, really, Alexa?

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:53.599
How about I talk to Google?"

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:56.869
"Google, turn on the lights!"

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.971
And she does.
-Wow. That's really nice.

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:01.374
They do say
set A.I. against each other.

00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:02.641
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:04.776
What a delight to have you
back here in person.

00:09:04.776 --> 00:09:08.079
It's always so great to see you.
You guys, that's Retta!

00:09:08.079 --> 00:09:11.417
"Ugliest House in America"
airs Sunday nights on HGTV

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.018
and streams on Discovery Plus.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:15.688
We'll be right back
with Iman Vellani, everybody.

